    "body": "fix on issue/3028-symlink-exe-posts · PR #3055 · pinned by data_dir::tests::a_symlinked_exe_finds_the_assets_beside_the_real_file, data_dir::tests::a_copied_exe_is_refused_with_the_fix · merges when reviewed\n\nLinux result (third \"Done means\" item). Release build of `camcraft-cli`, install-style folder outside a cargo build tree, `process examples/catalog/2d/first-part/first-part.camproj -o out.nc`:\n\n| Started as | Before the fix | With the fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| the installed file | rc 0, posted | rc 0, posted |\n| a symbolic link to it, in another folder | rc 0, posted | rc 0, posted (same bytes) |\n| a copy of it, in another folder | rc 1, \"no posts folder found\" | rc 1, same refusal, then a hint: start from the install folder or through a symbolic link |\n\nOn Linux, `std::env::current_exe` reads `/proc/self/exe`, which is already the real file. Thus a link worked on Linux before the fix. On macOS and Windows, `current_exe` gives the link path. The fix resolves a link before the lookup.\n\nWindows is not checked: I have no Windows machine. A reading on Windows is still necessary.\n\nI cannot set labels. Please set `in-review` on this issue if you agree.\n\n",
